<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernat I, Count of Besalú</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1020</span> · Also known as Bernat Tallaferro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernat I, called Tallaferro ('iron-cutter'), was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besalu">Besalú</a> from 988 to 1020 and a brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliba">Abbot Oliba</a>. He took part in the Catalan expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in 1010 and in 1017 obtained from the pope a bishopric for Besalú, which did not outlast him. He drowned crossing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> in 1020 on his way to Provence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernat-i-count-of-besalu.jpg" alt="Bernat I, Count of Besalú" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bernat_Tallaferro_and_Guillem_Bernat.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
